#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:1
msgid "Release 2.24.0 (2024-07-31)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:3
msgid "Significant changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:5
msgid "Harden user sandboxing"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:7
msgid ""
"The build directory has been hardened against interference with the outside "
"world by nesting it inside another directory owned by (and only readable by) "
"the daemon user."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:9
msgid ""
"This is a low severity security fix, [CVE-2024-38531](https://www.cve.org/"
"CVERecord?id=CVE-2024-38531)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:11
msgid ""
"Credit: [**@alois31**](https://github.com/alois31), [**Linus Heckemann "
"(@lheckemann)**](https://github.com/lheckemann) Co-authors: [**@edolstra**]"
"(https://github.com/edolstra)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:14
msgid ""
"`nix-shell <directory>` looks for `shell.nix` [\\#496](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/496) [\\#2279](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/2279) "
"[\\#4529](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/4529) [\\#5431](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/issues/5431) [\\#11053](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/11053) [\\#11057](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11057)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:16
msgid ""
"`nix-shell $x` now looks for `$x/shell.nix` when `$x` resolves to a "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:18
msgid ""
"Although this might be seen as a breaking change, its primarily interactive "
"usage makes it a minor issue. This adjustment addresses a commonly reported "
"problem."
msgstr ""

