msgid "Author: [**Winter (@winterqt)**](https://github.com/winterqt)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:168
msgid ""
"Rename hash format `base32` to `nix32` [\\#8678](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/8678)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:170
msgid ""
"Hash format `base32` was renamed to `nix32` since it used a special nix-"
"specific character set for [Base32](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base32)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:173
msgid "**Deprecation**: Use `nix32` instead of `base32` as `toHashFormat`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:175
msgid ""
"For the builtin `convertHash`, the `toHashFormat` parameter now accepts the "
"same hash formats as the `--to`/`--from` parameters of the `nix hash "
"convert` command: `\"base16\"`, `\"nix32\"`, `\"base64\"`, and `\"sri\"`. "
"The former `\"base32\"` value remains as a deprecated alias for `\"nix32\"`. "
"Please convert your code from:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:179
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.convertHash { inherit hash hashAlgo; toHashFormat = \"base32\";}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:183
msgid "to"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:185
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.convertHash { inherit hash hashAlgo; toHashFormat = \"nix32\";}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:189
msgid ""
"Add `pipe-operators` experimental feature [\\#11131](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/11131)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:191
msgid ""
"This is a draft implementation of [RFC 0148](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/"
"pull/148)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:193
msgid ""
"The `pipe-operators` experimental feature adds [`<|` and `|>` operators](../"
"language/operators.md#pipe-operators) to the Nix language. _a_ `|>` _b_ is "
"equivalent to the function application _b_ _a_, and _a_ `<|` _b_ is "
"equivalent to the function application _a_ _b_."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:197
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:207
msgid ""
"`<|` and `|>` are right and left associative, respectively, and have lower "
"precedence than any other operator. These properties may change in future "
"releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:210
msgid ""
"See [the RFC](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/pull/148) for more examples and "
"rationale."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:214
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` shebang uses relative path [\\#4232](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/4232) [\\#5088](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/5088) [\\#11058]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11058)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:217
msgid ""
"Relative [path](../language/types.md#type-path) literals in `nix-shell` "
"shebang scripts' options are now resolved relative to the [script's location]"
"(../glossary.md?highlight=base%20directory#gloss-base-directory). Previously "
"they were resolved relative to the current working directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:220
msgid "For example, consider the following script in `~/myproject/say-hi`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:230
msgid ""
"Older versions of `nix-shell` would resolve `shell.nix` relative to the "
"current working directory, such as the user's home directory in this example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:243
msgid ""
"Since this release, `nix-shell` resolves `shell.nix` relative to the "
"script's location, and `~/myproject/shell.nix` is used."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:250
msgid "**Opt-out**"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:252
msgid ""
"This is technically a breaking change, so we have added an option so you can "
"adapt independently of your Nix update. The old behavior can be opted into "
"by setting the option [`nix-shell-shebang-arguments-relative-to-script`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-nix-shell-shebang-arguments-relative-to-"
"script) to `false`. This option will be removed in a future release."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:258
msgid ""
"Improve handling of tarballs that don't consist of a single top-level "
"directory [\\#11195](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11195)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:260
msgid ""
"In previous Nix releases, the tarball fetcher (used by `builtins."
"fetchTarball`) erroneously merged top-level directories into a single "
"directory, and silently discarded top-level files that are not directories. "
"This is no longer the case. The new behaviour is that _only_ if the tarball "
"consists of a single directory, the top-level path component of the files in "
"the tarball is removed (similar to `tar`'s `--strip-components=1`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:264
msgid ""
"Setting to warn about large paths [\\#10778](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/10778)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:266
msgid ""
"Nix can now warn when evaluation of a Nix expression causes a large path to "
"be copied to the Nix store. The threshold for this warning can be configured "
"using the `warn-large-path-threshold` setting, e.g. `--warn-large-path-"
"threshold 100M`."
msgstr ""

